      "title": "Adjunct, Part-Time Teaching Positions",
      "description": "Adjunct, Part-Time Teaching Positions.  Augustana College is a selective liberal arts and sciences college of 2,500 students, including 26 percent first generation college students, 23 percent Pell Grant students, 24 percent students of color, and 12 percent international students. Our beautifully wooded and largely residential campus is located in Rock Island, IL, a diverse Illinois-Iowa Quad Cities metropolitan area along the Mississippi River with 400,000 residents about three hours west of Chicago. Strengthening our diverse and inclusive community is central to the college's mission and strategic plan. We seek applicants with an interest in fostering rigorous, inclusive, and high-impact learning environments for a diverse student body. Details about Augustana College, our expectations of the faculty, the selection process, and the Quad Cities all are available at Teaching at Augustana. Augustana College welcomes information from individuals interested in teaching on an adjunct or part-time basis in the future. Please submit your application materials, and we will contact you if a position in your area comes available. You can learn more about academic programs offered at Augustana at our website. Masters, doctoral, or terminal degree. The budgeted compensation for this position(s) is dependent upon enrollment at the below rates. (Compensation is contingent on meeting the enrollment threshold and is reduced if minimum enrollments are not met.) $1400 per credit for part-time instructors without a terminal degree. $1500 per credit for part-time instructors with a terminal degree. If scheduled for 13 credits or less per academic year, this position would not be benefits eligible. Augustana College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Augustana College provides equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, veteran status, and any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. Please submit a cover letter describing your teaching interest and experience and a curriculum vitae. We will contact you if a position in your area comes available. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $1,400 - $36,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859fa128817201a130dc922e782f": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - Office of the Registrar",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant - Office of the Registrar.  Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Administrative Assistant - Office of the Registrar Status: Full-time, non-Exempt position,12 month schedule Reports To: College Registrar Overview: Supports the College Registrar as well as overall activities of the Office. Works collaboratively with the other Administrative Assistant to ensure the needs of students, faculty, staff, administration and alumni constituents are met on a timely basis. Additionally, works with the degree audit and semester transition teams as needed through the calendar conversion. Primary Duties: Manages the tracking, production, mailing, transmittal and payment of all paper and electronic transcript requests. Answers phone calls from students, parents, faculty, other offices and either responds to the need or makes the appropriate referral. Process owner for application and on-boarding new non-degree students. Provides clerical and technical support to Registrar and Associate Registrar including writing letters, creating PowerPoint presentations, providing reports, maintaining meeting minutes and finding information from other offices to solve problems. Assists with oversight of the physical files for all students (past and present). Adds, deletes and updates information as requested by the Registrar or in accordance with the college’s record retention policy. Ensures all departmental processes, student records, and public-facing publications adhere to federal, state, and institutional guidelines (including FERPA and accreditation standards). Ensures strict compliance with federal, state, and institutional policies across all office workflows, official reporting, record keeping, and web publication processes. Manages the office calendars, schedules meetings and does event planning for the office. As the front line for the Office of the Registrar, assesses urgency of requests and ensures that those in need are put in touch with appropriate resources in a timely manner. Prioritizes the office workload and works collaboratively with the other assistant to oversee workload issues and assists in management of student workers to ensure maximum productivity and quality outcomes. Additional Duties: Collaborates with other staff, faculty and administration within the Academic Division, as well as other offices throughout the campus. Creates a welcoming environment for students, faculty, staff and alumni who seek the services of the office. Other duties as assigned. Competencies: Interpersonal communication Intercultural competency Office Technology Problem Solving Prioritization Skills & Experience: 3+ years of experience of related experience providing administrative support in a professional setting. Excellent oral and written communication skills, detail orientation and demonstrated organizational skills. Ability to work with confidential information. Ability to maintain calm and confident with students, faculty, coworkers or families in stressful situations. Intermediate working knowledge of Microsoft Office, Access and Excel. Experience with Colleague by Ellucian or other robust integrated database system is a definite plus. Ability to work with a diverse group of students and colleagues and members of the campus community. Excellent in-person and phone customer service skills and ability to maintain focus in a busy office environment. Ability to effectively prioritize and manage multiple priorities in an environment with frequent interruptions. Education: High school diploma or GED required. Additional education and/or experience highly preferred. Additional Information Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.50 - $17.00 per hour, commensurate with experience and qualifications. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Environment: This job operates in a professional office environment. This role routinely uses standard office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, filing cabinets and fax machines. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift 15 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, concentrate, and climb stairs, bend, and stoop. Must be able to use a telephone and computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Expected hours of work: This is a full time position with a 40 hour work week. Standard days and hours of work are Monday - Friday 8:00 am through 4:30 pm during the academic year as well as the summer months. Occasionally, and subject to supervisor approval, overtime may be required. Travel: Little to no travel is expected for this position. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $15.50 - $17.00 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7887a1a0f425da01a11710544b30da": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid.  Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Assistant Director of Financial Aid Wage Grade: 735 Status: Exempt, Full-time, 12-month schedule Reports To: Director of Financial Aid Primary Duties: The primary responsibilities of the Assistant Director of Financial Aid include assisting the Director in ensuring that aid is packaged in a timely manner for both current and incoming students in order to meet the goals of the institution. The packaging should be compliant with all federal, state and institutional policies. Additionally, the Assistant Director will work to maintain compliance with all policies tied to disbursement of student aid which will include coordination with other departments on campus including (but not restricted to) the Registrar’s Office, the Dean of Students Office and the Business Office. The Assistant Director should also be actively engaged in support of Admissions and the recruitment of new students as well as the support of all primary offices engaged with the retention of current students. Additional Duties: Assist in overseeing the management of state and federal need-based aid programs. Collaborate with Admissions and IT staff to submit the weekly prospective student data file to Encoura. Assist the Director of Financial Aid in compiling and submitting annual compliance reports. Other duties as assigned. Skills & Experience: 3-5 (or more) years of relevant work experience. Excellent written communication skills and demonstrated comfort with public speaking. Ability to develop rapport with a wide variety of student and family personalities. Strong cross-cultural and interpersonal communication skills. Commitment and ability to effectively communicate the value of the Augustana experience. Ability to manage multiple tasks and work with limited supervision. Good decision making and prioritization skills. Ability to effectively supervise student staff. Basic computer skills are required. Demonstrated ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Ability to represent the Augustana admissions team positively through a strong, student-centered focus. Education: Bachelor’s degree is required. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $45,000 - $50,000 annually commensurate with experience and qualifications. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Environment: This job operates in a hybrid office environment in accordance with institutional policy. Physical Demands: Must be able to lift 15 pounds on a frequent basis. Required ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Expected hours of work: 40 hours a week Travel: Little to no travel is required for this position. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Pay Range: $45,000 - $50,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7883a8a0abfc6b01a0cee7f0a10815": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager Dining Services",
      "description": "Assistant Manager Dining Services.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Assistant Manager Wage grade: 730 Status: Exempt, Full-time Reports To: General Manager of Gerber Dining Overview: To schedule, supervise, plan, direct and oversee the work of fulltime, temporary and student staff. Assists in managing all aspects of the production, presentation and service of quality food in Dining Services. Primary Duties: Assists, participates in and monitors the preparation and service of foods. Plans, coordinates and supervises the work activity of assigned support staff to assure proper staffing and consistent quality in operations. Pitches in regularly to meet deadlines and during times of staff shortage. Works with cooks and other dining services staff to insure that production of food occurs in a timely, safe and efficient manner and meets a high standard of quality. Works closely with other members of the dining services leadership team to resolve routine concerns and recommend measures to improve production/service methods, equipment performance, scheduling, quality control, and suggest changes in working conditions and use of equipment to increase efficiency and safety of the food service operations. Represents the interests of the College and of Dining Services leadership in the use of resources to meet service and productivity demands within unit goals and budgets; strives to promote continual process and quality improvement. Supervises and develops staff to minimize waste of food and create high levels of productivity. Maintains accurate records and generates reports to monitor production and service costs. Performs human resources functions including recruitment, interviewing, hiring, training, scheduling, evaluating, and disciplining of assigned fulltime and student staff. Communicates Augustana’s and Dining Services expectations. Oversees and maintains safety and sanitary standards in all service areas according to the Illinois Health Code and Augustana Dining Services standards. Communicates any concerns or changes to employees and takes responsibility for maintaining a safe and compliant working environment. Assures proper storage and labeling of food. Assures proper and safe use and maintenance of all equipment. Inspect and coordinate repairs and maintenance of equipment as required. Conducts a daily inventory of fresh food as well as other necessary items and places orders to maintain adequate supply. Looks for ways to proactively prevent waste and/or spoilage. Assists with monthly inventory, scheduling and payroll reporting as needed. Oversee operations as designated or in the absence of the General Manager. Actively participates in all catering or dining services special events to ensure high quality outcomes and a positive experience for guests. Conducts staff meetings with service staff. Participates in food service management team meetings and planning meetings; and other College and/or departmental meetings as assigned. Participates in departmental and personal professional growth activities. Responds to problems arising from inquiries and complaints from staff, students and the public. Additional Duties: Plan and assist for special events within Augustana Dining Services Assist in menu development Assist fulltime employees through peak service times Assists in the Retail & Catering Operations or with special events during peak periods. Performs various other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility: This position directly supervises 20+ employees per shift as well as a large group of student workers. Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of similar work experience in food preparation and supervision Must be proficient in computer software applications (e.g. Word, Excel, e-mail) Reasonable (1-3 years) experience with computerized food service management and POS systems and software Flexible attitude and willingness to perform all aspects of dining service operations during staffing shortages. Strong cross-cultural and interpersonal communication skills are necessary Ability to manage employees and student workers to create effective outcomes Good decision making and prioritization skills Demonstrated ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $42,000 - $46,000 per year, commensurate with experience and work history. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Education: High School Diploma or GED with one to three years of food service management experience. Demonstrated food service management, production experience and ServSafe Certification within three months of employment. Work Environment: This job operates in a professional food service environment. This role routinely uses commercial kitchen equipment such as rational ovens, steam kettles, bakery ovens, pizza ovens, and dish washers, along with basic office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, fax machines and filing cabinets. Schedule consists of a rotating day and evening shifts as well weekend shifts. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift 50 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Expected hours of work: Generally works shifts of 10am-7:30pm, 12pm-8:30pm or 1pm-9:30pm, including weekends. May occasionally work other 8 hours shifts between 6am -10pm to cover other shifts as needed. Will work a minimum of 40 hours per week. When academic classes are not in session and food service is not open, 8 hour shifts between 6am-5pm will be assumed, however occasional service demands may require a later end to shift. Travel: Little to no off campus travel is expected for this position. However, the Assistant Manager routinely assists with on campus food deliveries therefore candidates must possess a valid driver’s license and pass an MVR check. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Pay Range: $42,000 - $46,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7887a89efb878a019f24bf2459750b": {
      "title": "Assistant Nursing Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Nursing Professor.  Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences AN AFFILIATE OF AUGUSTANA COLLEGE Assistant Professor of Nursing About Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences is a private institution focused exclusively on nursing and health sciences education, serving students in the Quad Cities region and beyond. Located in Rock Island, the college is part of the bi-state Quad Cities metropolitan area along the Mississippi River, a regional hub for healthcare, education, and community partnerships. The College is an affiliate of Augustana College, and is in the process of a merger with Augustana College. Trinity offers undergraduate and graduate programs designed to prepare students for careers in nursing, health sciences, and healthcare leadership. Academic offerings include associate, bachelor’s, master’s, and certificate programs that emphasize evidence-based practice, clinical excellence, and compassionate patient care. In addition, Augustana College provides complimentary studies in Neuroscience, Communications Sciences and Disorders, Speech-Language Pathology, Kinesiology, Public Health, Pre-Nursing, Pre-Dentistry, Pre-Optometry, Pre-Medicine, Pre-Occupational Therapy, Pre-Pharmacy, and Pre-Physician Assistant. With a longstanding commitment to service, integrity, and academic excellence, our community fosters a supportive and student-centered learning environment where faculty and students build meaningful connections. The college seeks to prepare graduates who will make a positive impact in the communities they serve. The Position: Join the Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences faculty as an Assistant Professor of Nursing and help shape the next generation of nurses. In this role, you will teach undergraduate nursing students across didactic, laboratory, and clinical settings while fostering a supportive, inclusive, and high-quality learning environment. The Assistant Professor plans, implements, and evaluates learning experiences aligned with the Trinity College of Nursing and Health Sciences vision, mission, values, and program outcomes. Using innovative, evidence-based teaching strategies, you will promote critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and professional growth in future nurses committed to improving the health of individuals, families, and communities. This position fulfills the academic triad of teaching, scholarship, and service through active engagement in scholarly and service activities. The Assistant Professor contributes to curriculum development and continuous program improvement, collaborates with faculty and administration to support student success and accreditation requirements, and participates in assessment and quality improvement initiatives. Responsibilities: Demonstrates the behaviors aligned with the mission and vision of the College and adheres to policies and procedures and safety guidelines. Demonstrates ability to meet business needs of the department which includes regular, reliable attendance. Employee maintains current licenses and/or certifications required for the position. Practices and reflects knowledge of HIPAA, TJC, DNV, OSHA, FERPA, TITLE IX, and other federal/state regulatory agencies guiding higher education and healthcare. Completes all annual education and competency requirements within the calendar year. Is knowledgeable of College and department compliance requirements commensurate with position (Title IV, Title IX, Campus Violence). Brings any questions or concerns regarding compliance to the immediate attention of the supervisor. Takes appropriate action on concerns reported by department staff related to compliance. Supports vision, mission, and values of the College. What We're Looking For: Requirements: Education: An Associate Professor will have their MSN or terminal degree in Nursing Experience: 2 years of clinical practice License(s)/Certification(s): Registered Nurse license in both Iowa and Illinois or be eligible to do so Must possess and maintain current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification Why Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences? At Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences, you’ll join a collaborative and student-centered community dedicated to preparing the next generation of healthcare professionals. Small class sizes and close faculty-student relationships create an engaging learning environment where mentorship, innovation, and compassionate care are at the center of the educational experience. Faculty benefit from a supportive culture that values evidence-based teaching, interdisciplinary collaboration, and lifelong learning. Through strong partnerships with regional healthcare systems, educators have opportunities to connect classroom instruction with hands-on clinical experiences and emerging healthcare technologies. With more than a century of service to the Quad Cities community, we combine a rich tradition in healthcare education with a forward-looking commitment to innovation, diversity, integrity, and student success. Faculty are empowered to make a meaningful impact in the classroom, in clinical education, and throughout the broader healthcare community. More about the Relationship with Augustana College: On June 30, 2026, Augustana College acquired the assets of Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences. The full merger remains subject to approvals from relevant regulatory authorities, including the Department of Education, which is anticipated within approximately two years. Pending such approvals, Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences operates as a distinct educational institution and affiliate of Augustana College, while Augustana provides operational and administrative services to Trinity. Application Instructions: A complete application will include: A cover letter detailing interest in the position and understanding of teaching (limit 3 pages) Curriculum vitae Copy of relevant transcripts (unofficial is acceptable at this stage) A statement of teaching philosophy (limit 2 pages) Contact information for three references Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Misty D. Stick-Mueller at mistystickmueller@augustana.edu. The position will remain open until it is filled. To guarantee full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 1, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information The budgeted compensation for this position ranges from $65,000 to $68,000 per year based upon minimum and preferred qualifications, education, experience, skills, and abilities. Actual placement within the range will depend upon experience, education, research, rank, and other relevant factors. As an affiliate of Augustana College, benefits are provided by Augustana College and consist of a competitive and comprehensive benefit package to ensure our team is well cared for. Benefits include: Medical, Dental and Vision Insurance Retirement plan including eligibility to receive up to 7% contribution from the College. Company sponsored short-term and long-term disability benefits as use of college facilities including a wellness center, gym and recreation center. Tuition benefits for employees and their family members You can learn more about our benefits program at our Benefits Website. Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences and Augustana College are Equal Opportunity Employers. We provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, veteran status, and any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. Pay Range: $65,000 - $68,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859fa064222601a072c5cc774efb": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Physics.  Assistant Professor of Physics Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Description The Department of Physics, Engineering, and Astronomy at Augustana College, Rock Island, Illinois, invites applications for an Assistant Professor tenure-track position in Physics beginning in August of the 2027-2028 academic year. This is an exciting opportunity to join a department with well-established undergraduate programs in Physics, Engineering-Physics, Teaching Physics, and an ABET-accredited B.S. in General Engineering. Our new colleague will join a growing Physics, Engineering-Physics, Engineering, and Astronomy program. The successful candidate will teach 24 credits per 10-month academic year (standard courses are 4 credits) of introductory and upper-level physics courses and labs. The candidate is encouraged to contribute specialty courses related to their sub-field (particularly those that may be interdisciplinary) as well as contribute to the general education program. Preference will be given to experimentalists. The candidate will be expected to develop a research program appropriate for undergraduate involvement. Additionally, the successful candidate will participate in service to the department and the Augustana College community. Additional information about the department, including offered courses, may be found here. The candidate will join an active, ten-member department with disciplinary interests in thermal fluids, environmental fluid dynamics, 3D printing and design, signal processing, quantum photonics, nuclear physics, planetary and stellar magnetic fields, observational astronomy, physics education, and planetarium directing. The department houses research spaces for environmental fluid dynamics, computational fluid dynamics, nuclear physics, and quantum photonics. The department has a newly designed Maker Space with 3D printers, a laser cutter, a scanning electron microscope, a CNC mill, and a welding station. Instructional spaces include a newly renovated electronics lab, design lab, and studio physics teaching spaces. The department is committed to supporting candidates' professional development in research and teaching. Candidates will need to participate in interdisciplinary collaboration in teaching and/or research given the disciplinary diversity of the department. What we’re looking for Potential for teaching excellence Commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and the value of a broadly educated person Ability to recruit, engage, and mentor students of many backgrounds both in and out of the classroom Potential to meaningfully engage undergraduate students in an active research agenda Ability to contribute to the operation and development of the department and its programs Strengthen relationships across campus and with community partners Why Augustana? At Augustana, you'll find a supportive and collegial environment where faculty thrive professionally and personally. Our small class sizes foster deep connections between faculty and students. You'll have access to resources and opportunities to pursue innovative research and impactful teaching. Position Requirements Ph.D. in Engineering Physics, Physics, Applied Physics, Engineering, or a comparable field by August 26, 2027. ABD candidates will also be considered Ability to teach introductory and advanced classes in physics (including lab and lab courses) Ability to teach upper-level electives in physics or engineering, including electronics, advanced lab, and/or experimental design Ability to teach introductory courses in physics for non-major students Development of a research program that includes undergraduate students Commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration Application Instructions A complete application will include: Cover letter CV Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research agenda Copy of graduate transcripts Contact information for three references Current courses offered by the department are listed in the college catalog; please describe your background in scholarship and/or teaching of any of these classes in your cover letter. Questions may be directed to the chair of the department, Nathan Frank, at nathanfrank@augustana.edu. To guarantee full consideration, please submit all application materials by October 23, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Additional Information The budgeted compensation for this position ranges from $60,000 to $63,000 per year based upon minimum and preferred qualifications, education, experience, skills, and abilities. Actual placement within the range will depend upon experience, education, research, and other relevant factors. Augustana College offers a competitive and comprehensive benefit package to its employees to ensure our team is well cared for. Benefits include: Medical, dental and vision insurance Retirement plan including eligibility to receive up to 7% contribution from the College. Company sponsored short-term and long-term disability benefits as use of college facilities including a wellness center, gym and recreation center. Tuition benefits for employees and their family members. Pay Range: $60,000 - $63,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859fa064222601a072d71ae54f75": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Statistics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Statistics.  Assistant Professor of Statistics Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Description The Department of Math and Computer Sciences at Augustana College, Rock Island, Illinois, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning in August of the 2027-2028 academic year. The successful candidate will teach 24 credits per 10-month academic year (standard courses are 4 credits). Candidates should demonstrate enthusiasm for teaching statistics in both upper and lower-level statistics courses, as well as other mathematics or data science courses. Candidates should be interested in continuing a scholarly research agenda, and offer opportunities for undergraduate students to contribute to research projects. Candidates should be interested in advising undergraduate students majoring in statistics and/or data science The candidate will join five mathematicians and five computer scientists in an active joint Mathematics and Computer Science department. What We're Looking For The minimum requirement for this position is to hold a Ph.D. degree in statistics or mathematics (or be ABD). Successful candidates will demonstrate: Ability to teach lower-level and advanced statistics courses, such as Stats for Health Professionals, calculus-based Probability and Statistics, and Statistical Learning (for data scientists), especially in small classroom settings where hands-on active learning is prioritized. An interest in becoming an excellent teacher and/or the demonstrated potential for high quality teaching, especially in mathematics and statistics courses. Potential for successful research in a liberal arts environment, involving undergraduate students. Strong communication and organizational skills. Ability to recruit, work with, and motivate students both in and out of the classroom. The potential for interdisciplinary collaboration and the ability to contribute statistical expertise to programs and projects across the College. A commitment to active engagement in campus service and the scholarly vitality of the department and campus community. Why Augustana? At Augustana, you'll find a supportive and collegial environment where faculty thrive professionally and personally. Our small class sizes foster deep connections between faculty and students. You'll have access to resources and opportunities to pursue innovative research and impactful teaching. Application Instructions A complete application includes: A cover letter, expressing your interest in teaching within a liberal arts college like Augustana A curriculum vitae A copy of your graduate transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable at this stage) A statement of your teaching philosophy, including specific details of how that philosophy impacts your teaching at a practical level. A research statement, including a discussion of how you would involve undergraduate students your future research projects Contact information for three professional references. Questions may be directed to the chair of the department, Andrew Sward at andrewsward@augustana.edu. To guarantee full consideration, please submit all materials by October 16, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Additional Information The budgeted compensation for this position ranges from $60,000 to $63,000 per year based upon minimum and preferred qualifications, education, experience, skills, and abilities. Actual placement within the range will depend upon experience, education, research, and other relevant factors. Augustana College offers a competitive and comprehensive benefit package to its employees to ensure our team is well cared for. Benefits include: Medical, dental and vision insurance Retirement plan including eligibility to receive up to 7% contribution from the College. Company sponsored short-term and long-term disability benefits as use of college facilities including a wellness center, gym and recreation center. Tuition benefits for employees and their family members. You can learn more about our benefits program at our Benefits Website. Augustana College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Pay Range: $60,000 - $63,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7885a89f19777f019f2495b60f6c80": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Associate Professor of Nursing.  Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences AN AFFILIATE OF AUGUSTANA COLLEGE Associate Professor of Nursing About Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences: Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences is a private institution focused exclusively on nursing and health sciences education, serving students in the Quad Cities region and beyond. Located in Rock Island, the college is part of the bi-state Quad Cities metropolitan area along the Mississippi River, a regional hub for healthcare, education, and community partnerships. The College is an affiliate of Augustana College, and is in the process of a merger with Augustana College. Trinity offers undergraduate and graduate programs designed to prepare students for careers in nursing, health sciences, and healthcare leadership. Academic offerings include associate, bachelor’s, master’s, and certificate programs that emphasize evidence-based practice, clinical excellence, and compassionate patient care. In addition, Augustana College provides complimentary studies in Neuroscience, Communications Sciences and Disorders, Speech-Language Pathology, Kinesiology, Public Health, Pre-Nursing, Pre-Dentistry, Pre-Optometry, Pre-Medicine, Pre-Occupational Therapy, Pre-Pharmacy, and Pre-Physician Assistant. With a longstanding commitment to service, integrity, and academic excellence, our community fosters a supportive and student-centered learning environment where faculty and students build meaningful connections. The college seeks to prepare graduates who will make a positive impact in the communities they serve. The Position: Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences invites applicants for an Associate Professors of Nursing position, to help shape the next generation of nurses. In this role, you will teach undergraduate nursing students across didactic, laboratory, and clinical settings while fostering a supportive, inclusive, and high-quality learning environment. The Associate Professor plans, implements, and evaluates learning experiences aligned with the Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences vision, mission, values, and program outcomes. Using innovative, evidence-based teaching strategies, you will promote critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and professional growth in future nurses committed to improving the health of individuals, families, and communities. This position fulfills the academic triad of teaching, scholarship, and service through active engagement in scholarly and service activities. The Associate Professor contributes to curriculum development and continuous program improvement, collaborates with faculty and administration to support student success and accreditation requirements, and participates in assessment and quality improvement initiatives. Responsibilities: Demonstrates the behaviors aligned with the mission and vision of the College and adheres to policies and procedures and safety guidelines. Demonstrates ability to meet business needs of the department which includes regular, reliable attendance. Employee maintains current licenses and/or certifications required for the position. Practices and reflects knowledge of HIPAA, TJC, DNV, OSHA, FERPA, TITLE IX, and other federal/state regulatory agencies guiding higher education and healthcare. Completes all annual education and competency requirements within the calendar year. Is knowledgeable of College and department compliance requirements commensurate with position (Title IV, Title IX, Campus Violence). Brings any questions or concerns regarding compliance to the immediate attention of the supervisor. Takes appropriate action on concerns reported by department staff related to compliance. Supports vision, mission, and values of the College. What We're Looking For: Requirements: Education: An Associate Professor will have a Doctoral, Ph.D or terminal degree in Nursing Experience: 2 years of clinical practice License(s)/Certification(s): Registered Nurse license in both Iowa and Illinois or be eligible to do so Must possess and maintain current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Why Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences? At Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences, you’ll join a collaborative and student-centered community dedicated to preparing the next generation of healthcare professionals. Small class sizes and close faculty-student relationships create an engaging learning environment where mentorship, innovation, and compassionate care are at the center of the educational experience. Faculty benefit from a supportive culture that values evidence-based teaching, interdisciplinary collaboration, and lifelong learning. Through strong partnerships with regional healthcare systems, educators have opportunities to connect classroom instruction with hands-on clinical experiences and emerging healthcare technologies. With more than a century of service to the Quad Cities community, we combine a rich tradition in healthcare education with a forward-looking commitment to innovation, diversity, integrity, and student success. Faculty are empowered to make a meaningful impact in the classroom, in clinical education, and throughout the broader healthcare community. More about the Relationship with Augustana College: On June 30, 2026, Augustana College acquired the assets of Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences. The full merger remains subject to approvals from relevant regulatory authorities, including the Department of Education, which is anticipated within approximately two years. Pending such approvals, Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences operates as a distinct educational institution and affiliate of Augustana College, while Augustana provides operational and administrative services to Trinity. Application Instructions: A complete application will include: A cover letter detailing interest in the position and understanding of teaching (limit 3 pages) Curriculum vitae Copy of relevant transcripts (unofficial is acceptable at this stage) A statement of teaching philosophy (limit 2 pages) Contact information for three references Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Misty D. Stick-Mueller at mistystickmueller@augustana.edu. The position will remain open until it is filled. To guarantee full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 1, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information The budgeted compensation for this position ranges from $73,000 to $76,000 per year based upon minimum and preferred qualifications, education, experience, skills, and abilities. Actual placement within the range will depend upon experience, education, research, rank, and other relevant factors. As an affiliate of Augustana College, benefits are provided by Augustana College and consist of a competitive and comprehensive benefit package to ensure our team is well cared for. Benefits include: Medical, Dental and Vision Insurance Retirement plan including eligibility to receive up to 7% contribution from the College. Company sponsored short-term and long-term disability benefits as use of college facilities including a wellness center, gym and recreation center. Tuition benefits for employees and their family members You can learn more about our benefits program at our Benefits Website. Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences and Augustana College are Equal Opportunity Employers. We provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, veteran status, and any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. Pay Range: $73,000 - $76,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859f9de070d0019e1ccf8fea3f38": {
      "title": "Campus Chaplain and Director of Spiritual Life",
      "description": "Campus Chaplain and Director of Spiritual Life.  Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Campus Chaplain and Director of Spiritual Life Status: Full-time, Exempt position – 12-month work schedule Reports To: Vice President of Student Life and Dean of Students Overview: The Campus Chaplain and Director of Spiritual Life provides spiritual leadership to the campus community through efforts designed to cultivate connection, explore purpose and to intersect faith and learning. Successful candidates should bring experience working with young adults. This includes implementation of the college’s strategic directives as informed by the Five Faith Commitments of Augustana College and Rooted and Open: The Common Calling of the Network of ELCA Colleges and Universities. Augustana’s next Campus Chaplain will be called to lead a diverse and changing campus community in the promotion of spiritual health, wholeness and growth by means “deeply rooted in the Lutheran intellectual tradition and boldly open to insights from other religious and secular traditions” (Rooted and Open). This position will provide spiritual formation and educational leadership through planning and directing programs and activities related to ministry, service and vocational development, and the promotion of the mission, purpose and goals of Augustana College. Primary Duties: Provide pastoral care and spiritual guidance to the Augustana College community, with a particular focus on college students. Be an active, collaborative member of the Student Life division. Examples include participation in Orientation, Welcome Week, residential life programs, and student life events and meetings. Collaborate with departments across campus to develop and implement student programming to support the mission of Augustana College. Design (often with students and colleagues), coordinate and preside at worship services throughout the academic year. Build and lead a spiritual and religious life leadership team composed of students who work with the Chaplain in planning, coordinating, and implementing the campus ministry program. Foster campus conversations that build understanding of the Five Faith Commitments, Rooted and Open and similar documents informing the missional aspect of the shared life of the campus community. Nurture and promote the spiritual and worship lives of non-Lutheran and non-Christian students, including when desirable, inviting partnership with religious communities in the Quad Cities region, and serving as advisor to Interfaith student organizations. Develop campus ministry programming that engages a diverse student body, inviting students to examine their faith and spirituality through vocational reflection, service opportunities and Interfaith engagement. Serve as an active member of the planning, implementation, and execution of the ALIVE Program (Augustana Leaders in Vocational Exploration). Oversee, advise and as necessary organize designated spiritual life and service groups among students (e.g., Campus Cupboard), and serve as a partner or liaison to faculty / staff / community partners serving as advisors to such groups. Plan and oversee special commemorations and services for the campus community as appropriate, including traditional activities related to the opening and closing of the academic year, Homecoming, Advent, Yom HaShoah, and similar commemorations. Foster and provide support for the well-being and wellness of the College community, including serving as a liaison between the College and students/families in times of personal or family emergency. Organize retreats, service trips and civic engagement activities in alignment with the academic calendar. Encourage and as appropriate assist in planning programs and camps that bring pre-college students to the Augustana campus. Manage campus ministries staff and relevant budgets. In consultation with the Vice President of Student Life, partner with the Offices of Advancement and Admissions in activities that engage alumni and prospective students in the campus ministry program. Serve on the leadership team of the Presidential Center for Faith and Learning, acting as a liaison with the Vice President of Student Life. Serve on appropriate institutional and student life committees as assigned. Be an active participant in the colleague group of Chaplains at ELCA Colleges. Serve as a liaison to the ELCA, including as appropriate the congregations and synodical structures of the Northern Illinois and Southeast Iowa Synods. Perform other duties as may be assigned by the Vice President of Student Life. Skills and Experience: 3 to 5 years of ministry experience. Clear understanding of ministry in a college setting. Specifically, understanding the needs of current students. Familiarity with the traditions and values of Lutheran higher education, especially as understood in the ELCA. An ability to graciously lead Christian ministries within ecumenical and interfaith contexts. Culturally agile and proficient, and dedicated to culture and connection. Demonstrated administrative ability to work independently and make sound, timely decisions. Managerial and supervisory experience. Strong communication skills, both in writing and orally. Experience and comfort in using technologies and social media. Requirements: Master of Divinity or related Master’s degree required. Additional or advanced education (doctorate) and training is valued. An ordained Minister of Word and Sacrament in good standing with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America (ELCA), and eligible for the clergy roster of the Northern Illinois Synod. Work Environment: Work assignments may require working indoors and outdoors. Evening and weekend work will be required, albeit typically planned with appropriate notice. The exception would be during campus / world emergencies. Physical Demands: This position requires light physical effort. Position may require long periods of standing or walking, and may require frequent lifting of lightweight material. Travel: This position requires regular travel locally to engage with community partners and minimal, intermittent distance travel for Augustana and ELCA related meetings and business. Must be able to drive a vehicle. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: The hiring range for this position is $64,000 - $74,000 annually based on experience and qualifications. Candidates who meet clergy eligibility requirements may request that a portion of their compensation be designated as a housing allowance consistent with IRS regulations. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Application Instructions: For consideration, interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae, a copy of a delivered sermon including the context and audience (written, audio or video), and a one page professional philosophy / approach to the applicant’s vocation to serve as a College Chaplain and Director of Spiritual Life. Note: Augustana College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Augustana College provides equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, veteran status, and any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. Pay Range: $64,000 - $74,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78879ea06420fb01a0927cf2385d9f": {
      "title": "Career Coach: STEM & Environmental Careers",
      "description": "Career Coach: STEM & Environmental Careers.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Career Coach: STEM & Environmental Careers Status: Full-time, Exempt (12 month schedule) Wage Grade: 740 Reports To: Executive Director, Career and Professional Development Overview: Augustana’s distinctive model for experiential learning, first-year advising, and career and professional development, called CORE (Careers, Opportunities, Research, Exploration), supports students as they explore purpose, develop professional skills, gain relevant experience, and prepare for life after graduation. The Career Coach, STEM & Environment provides individualized career coaching, career-community engagement, instruction, and career-readiness programming for students pursuing opportunities in science, technology, engineering, mathematics, environmental studies, and related fields. The position also provides leadership and operational ownership for one or more assigned departmental programs or initiatives. Program assignments may evolve based on departmental priorities, institutional needs, and the employee’s skills and experience. Key Responsibility Areas Career Coaching and Career Community Engagement: 50% Provides individual and group career coaching in career exploration, professional preparation, experiential learning, job and graduate-school searches, and post-graduate planning. Helps students identify their interests, strengths, values, skills, and goals and translate them into educational, experiential, and career plans. Advises students on resumes, cover letters, professional profiles, networking, interviewing, job-search strategies, graduate and professional school preparation, and employment decisions. Serves students pursuing opportunities in science, technology, engineering, mathematics, environmental studies, and related fields and maintains current knowledge of relevant career paths, employment trends, hiring practices, and educational opportunities. Connects students with internships, research, job-shadowing opportunities, campus employment, alumni, employers, mentors, and other career-development experiences. Builds relationships with faculty, academic departments, alumni, employers, and community partners to support student referrals, outreach, and career-community connections. Collaborates with career coaches and campus partners to provide coordinated support and develops career resources responsive to student needs. Maintains accurate and timely records of coaching appointments, student engagement, referrals, and outcomes. Instruction, Workshops, and Facilitation: 25% Develops and delivers workshops, classroom presentations, and other career-development instruction. Teaches one or more Liberal Studies courses related to Career and Life Design, which may include advising a small cohort of transfer students, and completes associated instructional and advising responsibilities. Collaborates with faculty and departmental colleagues to develop relevant and scalable career-development content for specific courses, disciplines, and student populations. Incorporates Career and Life Design principles, career-readiness competencies, reflective practices, and professional skill development into instructional activities. Contributes to the development and pilot implementation of reflective and digital career-readiness tools, which may include student e-portfolios. Represents CORE through designated presentations and programs for students, prospective students, families, faculty, staff, and other campus audiences, including occasional evening, weekend, and summer events. Program Ownership and Coordination: 25% Provides operational ownership and coordination for one or more assigned career-development programs, services, or strategic initiatives. Develops annual goals, implementation plans, timelines, and priorities for assigned responsibilities in alignment with departmental and institutional objectives. Coordinates the day-to-day implementation of assigned programs, including scheduling, communication, participant engagement, resource development, and collaboration with partners. Develops and maintains procedures, resources, communication materials, and documentation needed for consistent and sustainable program delivery. Monitors participation, progress, feedback, and outcomes and uses available information to improve program effectiveness. Maintains accurate program records and prepares routine updates, summaries, and reports for department leadership. Manages multiple priorities, follows projects through completion, and ensures that assigned responsibilities remain current and responsive to student and institutional needs. Required Qualifications Experience providing career coaching, advising, counseling, mentoring, or comparable developmental support. Knowledge of career exploration, experiential learning, job-search practices, graduate education, or professional transitions. Ability to develop and deliver presentations, workshops, classroom instruction, and group activities. Demonstrated ability to coordinate programs involving multiple participants, partners, timelines, and communication needs. Ability to build effective relationships and collaborate with students, alumni, faculty, employers, and campus or community partners. Demonstrated ability to coordinate programs or projects involving multiple participants, partners, timelines, communications, and deliverables. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, and presentation skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Sound judgment and the ability to maintain confidentiality, establish professional boundaries, and make appropriate referrals. Strong organizational and time-management skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain accurate records. Ability to work independently and collaboratively and fulfill occasional evening, weekend, and summer responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with undergraduate students or young adults in a higher education setting. Understanding of Career Development and Life Design principles and the educational value of a liberal arts college. Knowledge of career paths, employment trends, graduate education, and professional expectations within STEM, environmental, or related fields. Experience coordinating a career-development, mentorship, faculty-engagement, employer-engagement, assessment, digital-content, or comparable student-success initiative. Experience working collaboratively with faculty, alumni relations, employers, or professional organizations. Experience using career-services technology, student-information systems, customer-relationship management systems, or comparable platforms. Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree in college student personnel, counseling, higher education, career development, social work, a STEM or environmental field, or a related field preferred. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $45,000 - $48,000 annually based on experience . We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Travel: This position is located on the Augustana College campus in Rock Island, Illinois, and involves limited travel. The employee must possess a current valid driver’s license and pass a motor vehicle record check. Special Requirements: As a staff member representing the College to students, families, alumni, employers, and community partners, this position requires excellent interpersonal skills, the ability to relate effectively to a diverse student body, and the ability and willingness to model the mission and standards of behavior of Augustana College. This position includes occasional evening and weekend responsibilities. All potential employees must pass a criminal background check. Physical Requirements: The physical demands described here are representative of those required to perform the essential functions of the position. The employee must be able to use a computer to complete job responsibilities and communicate effectively through individual meetings, group facilitation, classroom instruction, and public presentations. Work Environment: This position operates in a professional office and college-campus environment. The role routinely uses standard office equipment and technology and includes regular interaction with students, faculty, staff, alumni, employers, and community partners. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $45,000 - $48,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7883a8a0abfc6b01a0d6806f543d19": {
      "title": "Carver Center Director & Assistant Men's Basketball Coach",
      "description": "Carver Center Director & Assistant Men's Basketball Coach.  Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Carver Center Director & Assistant Men's Basketball Coach Status: Exempt, Combined full-time (75% Men's Basketball Coach, 25% Carver Center Director), academic year Reports To: Athletic Director & Head Men's Basketball Coach Overview: This position combines positions. As Carver Center Director, this position oversees the contest and practice schedule at the Carver Center, including all set-up and take-down requirements for home intercollegiate athletic contests in the building. As Assistant Coach, assists the head coach with recruiting, coaching and conditioning activities for the men's basketball program. Job Duties Carver Center Director (25%): 1. Manage facility calendars and communication of schedules for all Carver Center activities including, but not limited to, intercollegiate athletic events, practices, conferences and meetings; staffing, set- up and breakdown for events in accordance with league, conference and NCAA regulations; collaborating with various athletic department staff and coaches, external groups and vendors. 2. Serve as the liaison to other athletic department areas including, but not limited to, sports information, athletic training and equipment as it pertains to game day operations. 3. Assist with day- to- day maintenance of all athletic department facilities. 4. Supervision of game day staff required for set-up and take-down for home athletic contests and special events. 5. Apply critical thinking skills to assist Athletic Director with creation and implementation of strategies for event coordination and playing and practice season activities. 6. Other duties as assigned Assistant Men's Basketball Coach (75%): 1. Plan, conduct and evaluate practice activities for designated players. Provide group and individual assistance in a manner that engages the athletes and builds commitment to the program. 2. Work collaboratively with other members of the coaching staff to integrate efforts and create program success. Assist other staff members with activities as need to reach the goals of the team. 3. Meet with prospective students and their family members both on campus and at remote locations. Provide advice and counsel on the admissions process, the Augustana experience and the integral role of the student athlete in overall campus life. 4. Provide feedback to assigned staff members and student workers on work performance and overall effectiveness. 5. Create teaching curriculums for physical education activity courses as assigned during the academic year. Find ways to engage students in learning activities. 6. Other duties as assigned Requirements: Education: Bachelor's degree required, MA preferred in a related field. Experience & Skills: 3 or more years' experience in a coaching role. Experience in small college athletics is highly preferred. Ability to understand and comply with a variety of regulations from the NCAA as well as other regulatory bodies. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to interact with a diverse group of coaches, administrators, student athletes, prospective students and families, and other members of the campus community. Strong prioritization and organizational skills. Must have a thorough understanding of and accountability to NCAA and CCIW rules and regulations. Strong commitment to the academic and athletic success of the student athlete. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: Starting salary for this role is $40,000 to $55,000 per year, depending on qualifications and relevant experience. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Hours & Travel: This position requires travel to away games during the season and to high school games, events, and other opportunities to meet with prospective students. Extended weekend and evening hours especially during the basketball season are expected. Current valid driver's license required. Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift 50 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Exposure to outside weather and extreme temperatures is occasionally required. Long work days, particularly during the recruiting and competition season on a frequent basis. Special Requirements: As key personnel representing the College, this position requires excellent interpersonal skills, the ability to relate to a diverse population, and the ability and willingness to model the mission and high standard of behavior of Augustana College. Successful candidates must pass a criminal background check. Successful candidates must pass a criminal background check and have a valid drivers' license with the ability to be insured by the college. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $40,000 - $55,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859e9f4435ab019f4d5f5802789e": {
      "title": "Cook - Academic Year Schedule",
      "description": "Cook - Academic Year Schedule.  Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Cook Wage Grade: 715 Status: Non-Exempt, Full-time, 10 month schedule, additional summer work may be available Reports To: Executive Chef Overview: Under direct supervision, performs general cooking duties using standardized recipes and instructions as needed to prepare hot and cold food items for dining center, retail and catering. Primary Duties: Prepares hot and cold food items for dining center service or catering events. Adapts to special requests and dietary concerns of individuals upon request. Interacts with guests at food stations while preparing and serving foods according to the menu, providing information and soliciting feedback from guests and ensuring a high quality experience. Works with other cooks and dining services staff to insure that production of food occurs in a timely, safe and efficient manner and meets a high standard of quality. Records production for each shift making suggestions and/or communicating concerns on a daily basis. Works to minimize waste of food and meets high levels of productivity. Adheres to standardized recipes Follows safety and sanitation standards set by state, federal and Augustana Dining Service’s rules and regulations. Works with other staff to produce necessary food products to meet deadlines. Collaborates with team members in a positive manner to achieve Dining Service’s objectives. Assist in providing on the job training and assists in directing the work of food service staff, including students within area of assignment. Notifies supervisor of food and supplies needed and when equipment or facilities are in need of repair. Performs other related preparation and sanitation duties as assigned. Works multiple stations within the Gerber Dining Center. Performs various other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of demonstrated experience in food preparation in a commercial setting or equivalent food service experience preferred. Minimum one year continuous employment in past position. Ability to work with limited supervision and in collaboration with other employees. Ability to work quickly and efficiently in a high volume, customer-oriented environment. Outstanding service orientation and the ability to create immediate rapport with a wide variety of personalities. Education: High School diploma or equivalent. Culinary training preferred. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.00 per hour. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Environment: This job operates in a professional food service environment. This role routinely uses commercial kitchen equipment such as rational ovens, stem kettles, bakery ovens, pizza ovens, and dish washers, along with basic office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, fax machines and filing cabinets. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift 50 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must possess finger and hand dexterity for using small tools and equipment. Expected hours of work: Generally works shifts of 6am-2:30pm or 11:30am-8pm, including weekends. Typically rotates one week am and the next week pm. Rotating weekends off when possible. Work hours and schedule is driven by department's operational need. May occasionally work other 8 hours shifts or overtime between 6am -10pm to cover for special events, peak periods of operation and staff shortages. When academic classes are not in session and food service is not open you may work an 8 hours shift between 6am-5pm. Travel: Little to no travel is expected for this position. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Pay Range: $15 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859e9fd3bb25019ff2cf40640f8c": {
      "title": "Manager of Grants & Corporate Relations",
      "description": "Manager of Grants & Corporate Relations.  Make an Impact at Augustana College An Augustana education is bold, boundless and life-changing - for students and the people who help shape their journeys. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships - the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). With 2,500 students, Augustana is a place where mentorship matters, innovation thrives, and every role contributes to student success. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek dynamic professionals who are passionate about shaping futures and who thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education. If this is you, we invite you to join us at Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Manager of Grants & Corporate Relations Status: Exempt, Full-time, 12-month work schedule Wage Grade: 735S Reports To: Director of Grants Management Overview: This position will be responsible for fundraising through grant writing and other corporate and foundation activities for Augustana College (75%) and WVIK Quad Cities NPR (25%). They will reside in the Office of Advancement. Advancement staff works with alumni, parents, friends, corporations and foundations to engage them in the mission of the college and encourage philanthropy that advances the goals of Augustana's strategic plan. The manager of grants and corporate relations writes and coordinates grants and proposals to corporations and foundations with guidance from the Director of Grants Management and Vice President for College Advancement in support of Presidential priorities, capital projects, and academic priorities of the Provost. The manager will also conduct and participate in similar activities in support of WVIK. Job Duties: Collect content, write, edit, and/or support submission of annual grant proposals to corporations, foundations and government funding sources on a variety of topics ($1,000 - $1 million) for Augustana and WVIK Maintain an operational calendar of submissions and reports Write and compile grant reports Work with faculty, staff, and administrators across campus to gather and interpret information for grant proposals and reports Work with the Business Office to discuss and resolve questions pertaining to grant funds and budgets Research local and national trends in corporate and foundation philanthropy, higher education, and public radio, and maintain a broad and deep knowledge of specific campus programs and projects Identify new funding opportunities that match college and WVIK fundraising priorities Handle and discuss confidential information appropriately Participate in and support the overall efforts of the Advancement office by assisting with projects and events as needed Other duties as assigned Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of demonstrated grant writing, professional writing or related experience Strong writing, editing, project management, and organizational skills Succeeds at planning and managing multiple projects with deadlines under limited supervision Proven computer skills with intermediate to advanced knowledge of Google Suite, Microsoft Word and Excel Ability to understand program and project content in academic and student life, and public radio Capable of communicating effectively with a diverse group of grantors, faculty and colleagues Thrives in a team project environment that adheres to specific deadline driven tasks and goals Succeeds at handling confidential information appropriately Commitment to the mission of Augustana College and WVIK Quad Cities NPR Additional Duties: Annually review processes and procedures for efficiency and improved outcomes Work collaboratively with other members of the Office of Advancement, WVIK, and other campus offices, on fundraising and engagement projects as appropriate Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $46,000 - $53,000 annually based upon skills, experience and abilities. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Environment: This job operates in a professional office environment. This role routinely uses standard office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, and filing cabinets. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to sit for long periods of time. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read and write. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Expected hours of work: This is a full-time position with a 40-hour work week. Standard days and hours of work are Monday – Friday 8:00 a.m. through 4:30pm. Must be available during key Advancement Office events: A Day of Giving, Giving Tuesday, Homecoming, Parents’ Weekend. Travel: This position has little to no travel requirements. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $46,000 - $53,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7885a8a0abfd5001a0f08fef081b93": {
      "title": "Public Safety Dispatcher",
      "description": "Public Safety Dispatcher.  Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Public Safety Dispatcher Status: Non-Exempt, 12 month, 32 hours per week (.75FTE) Wage Grade: 720 Reports To: Chief of Police Overview: Provide dispatch services and additional support to College community. This position is part of a team that provides 24 hours per day, 7 days per week, 365 days per year coverage. This is a part time (75%) 12-month position, rotating 2nd shift (3pm – 11pm) and 3rd shift (11p-7am) with rotating weekend/holiday responsibilities. This position works 4 days each week. Job Duties: Answers calls received at the switchboard. Based on information provided by the caller, route calls to the appropriate party and/or dispatch security officers to respond. Monitors fire alarms, responding according to College policy and protocol. Monitors camera feeds and reacts to situations as necessary. Calls in facilities service personnel and other Augustana employees for emergency purposes or as instructed. Answers emergency calls and notifies appropriate internal and external parties as specified by College policy and protocol. Sends electronic notifications via E2 Campus system to alert campus community of safety concerns. Issues visitor and temporary parking passes. Check in contractors. Performs additional administrative support duties as requested. Other duties as assigned Education: High School Diploma or GED required. Experience & Skills: Excellent verbal and written communication skills and the ability to use Microsoft Office products to create written documents. Strong proficiency utilizing desktop PC’s (Personal Computers) Ability to remain calm during emergency and stressful situations Ability to make decision with limited supervision and extreme time constraints. Ability to work with a diverse group of colleagues, students, and campus visitors. Ability to work efficiently with frequent interruptions. Travel: None Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift 25 pounds on a frequent basis Also required is the ability to see, listen, hear, speak, read, bend, stoop, and use a computer and telephone to accomplish work outcomes. Additional Requirements: This position requires a valid driver’s license. Successful candidates must complete a criminal background check. Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.45 per hour. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Note: This job description is subject to change and is not designed to be a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required by the employee. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College's policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Pay Range: $15.45 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78839ea0f4259801a116b0447b286f": {
      "title": "Public Safety Support Officer",
      "description": "Public Safety Support Officer.  Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Public Safety Support Officer Status: Non-Exempt, Part-time, 10 Month Schedule Wage Grade: 710 Reports To: Chief, Augustana Police Department Overview: Provide security services to College academic buildings and property to protect against fire, theft and illegal entry. This position includes overnight hours (generally 8pm – 2am). Essential Duties: Responsible for following established procedures for touring academic buildings and Augustana College property. Stays in contact with other security personnel reporting breakage or other irregularities. Ensures that doors, entrances and other access points are locked and secured according to established policies. Turns off unneeded lights as scheduled. Assist campus visitors and ensures that visitors are on campus for appropriate reasons. Reports unsafe conditions or suspicious persons to Dispatcher and Security Officers. Responds to, and provides approved requests for access in academic buildings. Other duties as assigned Education: High School Diploma or equivalent required. Experience & Skills: Prior security or military experience preferred Willingness to learn and accept instruction and follow established procedures Ability to work with limited supervision and in extreme weather conditions Ability to work with a diverse group of colleagues, faculty members and students Travel: None Work Environment: This position is regularly exposed to inside and outside. Frequent exposure to extreme heat and cold weather conditions. Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift 25 pounds on a frequent basis. This position requires good physical condition with the ability to walk for long periods and climb stairs in an outdoor environment. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Additional Requirements: This position requires a valid driver’s license. Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.00/hour. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Access to a voluntary retirement savings plan administered through TIAA (employee-contributed Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Augustana College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Augustana College provides equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, veteran status, and any other category protected by federal, state, or local law. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a resume and cover letter. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $15 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
