    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7887a89f8b9426019fa4485ed31e59": {
      "title": "Student Success Program Assistant",
      "description": "Student Success Program Assistant.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Student Success Program Assistant Wage Grade: 730 Status: Non-Exempt, full-time, 12 month position. Reports to: Associate Vice President of Retention and Student Success Supervises: Student Workers Overview: The Student Success Program Assistant in the Learning Commons plays a vital role in advancing student success at Augustana College. The Learning Commons is an integrated hub of academic support services —including Disability & Access Resources, the Reading/Writing Center, the STEM/Q Center, Student Success & Advising Services, and TRIO—designed to help every student maximize their potential. As the welcoming first point of contact, you will foster a supportive and inclusive environment for students seeking academic guidance, tutoring, and skill development. This role supports daily operations, manages program logistics, supervises student workers, coordinates communications, and assists professional staff and faculty in delivering high-quality academic support. This position is ideal for someone who enjoys variety, thrives in a collaborative environment, and finds satisfaction in helping others succeed. Successful candidates are warm, student-centered, tech-savvy, organized, detail-oriented, proactive, and enthusiastic about working with a diverse student population. Key Responsibilities Serve as the welcoming presence of the Learning Commons; greet visitors, answer inquiries, and ensure that all students feel included and supported. Respond to emails, phone calls, and service-area questions promptly and professionally. Maintain an organized and efficient office environment; oversee scheduling, room reservations, and event logistics. Support student success initiatives by assisting with early alert tracking and follow-up in Early Alert software (Starfish). Update Early Alert (Starfish) feature configuration as necessary, perform semester transition activities, ensure peer leaders, tutors, and coaches are configured for Learning Commons services, and collaborate with the Starfish technical lead in ITS to troubleshoot issues as they arise. Support Disability and Access Resources Testing Center as requested. Assist with new student Orientation and Registration processes. Support Augie Mentor Program as needed. Assist with peer leader, peer tutor and peer academic coach recruiting, hiring, and scheduling. Recruit, hire, train, and supervise student employees who serve as Learning Commons administrative support staff. Foster a positive and inclusive team culture among student employees and create a meaningful on-campus work experience that builds professional skills. Coordinate payroll for student workers (peer academic coaches, peer leaders, peer tutors, and other Learning Commons staff). Facilitate departmental financial management, including P-card reconciliation and invoice processing. Maintain standard operating procedures for key Learning Commons functions. Maintain and update Learning Commons webpages and social media to promote resources and events. Participate in Learning Commons staff meetings and contribute ideas to improve operations and student outreach. Assist with special projects, events, and student success initiatives as assigned. Required Qualifications Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment with accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills; ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and families from diverse backgrounds. Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace, and comfort learning new systems such as Starfish, budget management software, virtual conference programs, and web content management tools. Strong organizational and problem-solving skills; able to anticipate needs and propose solutions. Demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive, student-centered environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience in student support in an educational setting. Experience supervising or mentoring student employees. Familiarity with accessibility/disability services, tutoring programs, or TRIO initiatives. Experience maintaining web content or managing departmental social media accounts. Education: Associate’s degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $18.77 - $23.46 per hour, commensurate with experience and qualifications. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $18.77 - $23.46 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859e9fd3bb2501a03b7dee7b0cc5": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager Dining Services",
      "description": "Assistant Manager Dining Services.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Assistant Manager Wage grade: 730 Status: Exempt, Full-time Reports To: General Manager of Gerber Dining Overview: To schedule, supervise, plan, direct and oversee the work of fulltime, temporary and student staff. Assists in managing all aspects of the production, presentation and service of quality food in Dining Services. Primary Duties: Assists, participates in and monitors the preparation and service of foods. Plans, coordinates and supervises the work activity of assigned support staff to assure proper staffing and consistent quality in operations. Pitches in regularly to meet deadlines and during times of staff shortage. Works with cooks and other dining services staff to insure that production of food occurs in a timely, safe and efficient manner and meets a high standard of quality. Works closely with other members of the dining services leadership team to resolve routine concerns and recommend measures to improve production/service methods, equipment performance, scheduling, quality control, and suggest changes in working conditions and use of equipment to increase efficiency and safety of the food service operations. Represents the interests of the College and of Dining Services leadership in the use of resources to meet service and productivity demands within unit goals and budgets; strives to promote continual process and quality improvement. Supervises and develops staff to minimize waste of food and create high levels of productivity. Maintains accurate records and generates reports to monitor production and service costs. Performs human resources functions including recruitment, interviewing, hiring, training, scheduling, evaluating, and disciplining of assigned fulltime and student staff. Communicates Augustana’s and Dining Services expectations. Oversees and maintains safety and sanitary standards in all service areas according to the Illinois Health Code and Augustana Dining Services standards. Communicates any concerns or changes to employees and takes responsibility for maintaining a safe and compliant working environment. Assures proper storage and labeling of food. Assures proper and safe use and maintenance of all equipment. Inspect and coordinate repairs and maintenance of equipment as required. Conducts a daily inventory of fresh food as well as other necessary items and places orders to maintain adequate supply. Looks for ways to proactively prevent waste and/or spoilage. Assists with monthly inventory, scheduling and payroll reporting as needed. Oversee operations as designated or in the absence of the General Manager. Actively participates in all catering or dining services special events to ensure high quality outcomes and a positive experience for guests. Conducts staff meetings with service staff. Participates in food service management team meetings and planning meetings; and other College and/or departmental meetings as assigned. Participates in departmental and personal professional growth activities. Responds to problems arising from inquiries and complaints from staff, students and the public. Additional Duties: Plan and assist for special events within Augustana Dining Services Assist in menu development Assist fulltime employees through peak service times Assists in the Retail & Catering Operations or with special events during peak periods. Performs various other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility: This position directly supervises 20+ employees per shift as well as a large group of student workers. Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of similar work experience in food preparation and supervision Must be proficient in computer software applications (e.g. Word, Excel, e-mail) Reasonable (1-3 years) experience with computerized food service management and POS systems and software Flexible attitude and willingness to perform all aspects of dining service operations during staffing shortages. Strong cross-cultural and interpersonal communication skills are necessary Ability to manage employees and student workers to create effective outcomes Good decision making and prioritization skills Demonstrated ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $42,000 - $46,000 per year, commensurate with experience and work history. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Education: High School Diploma or GED with one to three years of food service management experience. Demonstrated food service management, production experience and ServSafe Certification within three months of employment. Work Environment: This job operates in a professional food service environment. This role routinely uses commercial kitchen equipment such as rational ovens, steam kettles, bakery ovens, pizza ovens, and dish washers, along with basic office equipment such as computers, phones, photocopiers, fax machines and filing cabinets. Schedule consists of a rotating day and evening shifts as well weekend shifts. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift 50 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Expected hours of work: Generally works shifts of 10am-7:30pm, 12pm-8:30pm or 1pm-9:30pm, including weekends. May occasionally work other 8 hours shifts between 6am -10pm to cover other shifts as needed. Will work a minimum of 40 hours per week. When academic classes are not in session and food service is not open, 8 hour shifts between 6am-5pm will be assumed, however occasional service demands may require a later end to shift. Travel: Little to no off campus travel is expected for this position. However, the Assistant Manager routinely assists with on campus food deliveries therefore candidates must possess a valid driver’s license and pass an MVR check. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Pay Range: $42,000 - $46,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78839fa0f425e701a11c58717264f3": {
      "title": "Athletic Field Specialist",
      "description": "Athletic Field Specialist.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Athletic Field Specialist - Grounds Wage Grade: 710 Status: Full-time, Non-exempt position - 12 month work schedule Reports to: Grounds Manager Overview: Under general direction of the Grounds Manager the Athletic Field Specialist oversees the daily maintenance of all Augustana athletic playing surfaces, turf areas and general grounds. During winter months, the incumbent will be assigned to Groundskeeper duties to assist with overall campus maintenance and snow removal. This position requires specialized knowledge of both natural and synthetic athletic turf maintenance. Primary Duties: Maintain natural and synthetic athletic fields throughout the Athletic Department. Re-groom and rebuild, when necessary, pitcher’s mounds, including clay repair; make soil amendments; drag and groom infield areas; inspect and maintain proper playing field levels to minimize lips; and apply appropriate materials as needed. Groom synthetic fields, including topdressing, raking and redistributing rubber infill, and spot sanitizing. Preferred previous experience with the maintenance and operation of large-scale irrigation systems. Set up and break down playing surfaces for practices, home games, and other athletic events. Perform turf maintenance operations on all campus turf, including but not limited to mowing, trimming, aerating, fertilizing, and weed control. Assist Groundskeepers with maintaining campus grounds and facilities. Assist with facility preparation, setup, and cleanup for departmental events. Collect and properly dispose of outdoor trash and recyclable materials. Maintain appropriate inventory of supplies and materials and oversee scheduled maintenance of equipment with assistance from the Motorpool Technician. Utilize equipment, tools, and chemicals in a safe and responsible manner, consistent with training, established safety procedures, and manufacturers’ recommendations. Operate large motorized equipment, including 40 HP tractors, skid steers, all-terrain vehicles, forklifts, aerial lifts, and applicable attachments, to complete routine and specialized job assignments. Ensure that campus community members receive quality service and timely responses to requests. Identify, evaluate, and communicate issues that require additional attention and coordinate appropriate follow-up to ensure timely resolution. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the Grounds and Athletic Departments. Additional Duties: Works with other campus community members and leaders on special projects. Oversees student workers as assigned ensuring high productivity and professional behavior. Other duties as assigned. Skills & Experience: 3–5 years of experience working with college, school district, golf course, or professional-level sports fields. Demonstrated ability to calculate fertilizer and chemical application rates. Experience operating specialized turf equipment, such as sprayers, spreaders, aerators, mowers, blowers, edgers, and similar equipment. Experience maintaining clay surfaces for baseball and/or softball. Knowledge of synthetic turf maintenance is a plus. Flexible attitude and willingness to perform all aspects of the job during periods of high workload, emergencies, and/or staffing shortages. Proficiency in using a computer to communicate and complete work-related tasks. Ability to work with limited supervision, work effectively independently, and contribute as part of a team. Currently possess a State of Illinois Pesticide License or ability to obtain one within 120 days of hire. Valid driver’s license and clean Motor Vehicle Record (MVR) required. Education: High School Diploma or GED and 3–5 years of experience in athletic field and/or golf course maintenance required. Degree or certification in Turf Management, Sports Field Management, or a related field preferred. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.00 per hour, commensurate with experience and qualifications. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Environment: This position operates primarily outdoors and requires exposure to extreme heat, cold, and varying weather conditions. The ability to work outdoors in a variety of weather conditions is essential to performing the duties of this position. Work Hours: This position is considered essential to the operations of the College. As such, the incumbent is expected to report to work even when the College is closed due to severe weather or other emergency conditions. The incumbent must be available and prepared to report to work with very short notice, as operational needs may arise at any time of day or night. An on-call rotation with irregular and variable hours will be required during various times of the year to meet the operational demands of the College. Physical Demand: The physical demands described below are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Must be able to regularly lift and carry up to 50 pounds unassisted with the ability to position, maneuver and transport objects weighing up to 100 pounds using proper material handling equipment and team-lift procedures. Must be able to frequently push and pull heavy machinery and equipment. Must be able to listen, hear, speak, read, and write effectively. Must be able to bend, stoop, kneel, and stand for extended periods of time. Must possess sufficient finger and hand dexterity to safely and effectively operate small tools and equipment. Requires frequent walking and climbing of stairs, as well as occasional work from ladders. A College-provided uniform is required and must be worn as directed. Steel-toed footwear is required while performing job duties. College assisted payment plan Expected hours of work: Monday through Friday, 7:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. Additional hours and schedule adjustments may be required during inclement weather or as operational needs dictate. Travel: Extensive travel throughout campus is expected, as this position requires frequent movement between multiple on-campus locations throughout the workday. Travel may cover a campus area within an approximately three-mile radius. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $15 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7887a8a03fc2be01a0640bf2951f16": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant - Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Executive Assistant - Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs.  Our Academic Affairs team is seeking an internal candidate to spearhead faculty and campus-wide communications while serving as the primary planner for our annual Commencement activities. In this role, you will collaborate closely with academic support staff to drive essential operations and deliver our institution's most celebrated traditions. Job Title: Executive Assistant to the Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Status: Non-exempt, Full-time 12 month schedule Wage Grade: 730 Reports To: Provost of the College Overview: The Executive Assistant to the Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs provides administrative support to the college’s chief academic officer and general support to the Academic Affairs team. This position plays a critical role in the work of Academic Affairs which ensures academic quality, supports faculty, and encourages and leads academic initiatives and innovation across the college. The Executive Assistant has primary responsibility for coordinating the Provost's calendar and performing a wide range of administrative functions to support the broader mission and ensure smooth day-to-day operations. This position reports to the Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs. The ideal candidate will be experienced in handling a broad range of activities and will be able to work independently, proactively, and collaboratively. They must be well organized and flexible and enjoy the administrative challenges of supporting an office with diverse constituents and needs. The position requires the ability to interact diplomatically and efficiently with a broad range of individuals, including faculty, students, administrators, external colleagues, and visitors. They will be comfortable working to deadlines and remaining flexible, proactive, resourceful, and professional. Excellent communication skills, a high degree of discretion, a commitment to providing excellent service and building positive working relationships, and attention to details are equally important. Job Duties: Manage the Provost’s calendar and flow of visitors and appointments, including scheduling reviews related to faculty personnel, job candidate, and departmental reviews. Manage workflow for faculty searches and external program reviews. Manage the Provost’s Office general email account, drafting communications and redirecting enquiries as appropriate, and manage the general Provost’s Office phone line, redirecting calls as needed. Act as a point person in the Provost’s Office for ensuring efficient operations and smooth flow of information both within the Provost’s Office and with colleagues across the College; coordinate these efforts with colleagues in the President's and Provost's Offices, as well as colleagues in divisional offices, and especially coordinate shared responsibilities with the Executive Assistant to the President. Assist in organizing / coordinating various events hosted by Academic Affairs. Provide proactive administrative support to the Provost and Associate Deans in the Office of Academic Affairs. Welcome and assist visitors to the Academic Affairs office either in person or via telephone. Provide administrative support including but not limited to; writing letters, preparing responses to correspondence, and creating meeting agendas and maintaining minutes. Assists with special projects by serving as the project manager, setting goals, monitoring progress, staying within budget and meeting assigned deliverables. Other administrative support duties as assigned Skills & Experience: 3+ years of administrative support experience or related experience in a professional setting including K-12, medical, or other related fields. Ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise good judgment, and act professionally, sensitively, and with a high level of discretion. Ability to anticipate needs and work proactively and collaboratively to manage daily flow of the office. Excellent interpersonal skills and commitment to collaborative teamwork Strong verbal and written communication skills Strong detail orientation and demonstrated organizational skills Ability to work independently Strong proficiency with technology, including Apple and PC hardware and software (especially Google Apps, Microsoft Office). Commitment to equity and inclusion in working in a diverse community of students and colleagues Ability to effectively prioritize and manage multiple priorities in an environment with frequent interruptions. Education: High school diploma or GED required. Additional education and/or experience in a college or university setting highly preferred. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $18.75 - $19.50 hour depending on experience and qualifications. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift 15 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, concentrate, climb stairs, bend, and stoop. Must be able to use a telephone and computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $18.75 - $19.50 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859fa064222601a072af25d04e51": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English (pre-1800s British Literature)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of English (pre-1800s British Literature).  Assistant Professor of English (pre-1800s British Literature) Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Description The Department of English at Augustana College, Rock Island, Illinois, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English specializing in pre-1800 British literature beginning in August of the 2027-28 academic year. This is an exciting opportunity to join a department with a well-established undergraduate program in literature, creative writing, English education, and publishing. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses in a liberal arts context in early British literature, Shakespeare, and first-year writing, with opportunities to design courses aligned with your expertise; Carry a teaching load of 24 credits per 10-month academic year (standard courses are 4 credits); Engage in mentorship with students in the program and actively contribute to the inclusive and innovative teaching practices that define Augustana's learning environment; Contribute to departmental and college-wide conversations about writing pedagogy, AI, and writing across the curriculum; Engage in scholarly activity, with institutional support from a pre-tenure paid leave and competitive research/travel grants. What We're Looking For Expertise in pre-1800s British literature, with a doctorate or ABD in English; Enthusiasm for teaching writing and expertise in AI and writing pedagogies; Potential for and commitment to excellence in teaching and mentorship; A commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration and the value of a broadly educated person; Potential for continued scholarly publication in fields of interest; Ability to understand, respect and support the work of other colleagues. Why Augustana? At Augustana, you'll find a supportive and collegial environment where faculty thrive professionally and personally. Our small class sizes foster deep connections between faculty and students. You'll have access to resources and opportunities to pursue innovative research and impactful teaching. Position Requirements Expertise in pre-1800s British literature, with a doctorate or ABD in English Ability to teach lower-division British literature classes (including a survey of British literature, Shakespeare in Film, and a special topics class) in a liberal arts context Ability to teach advanced Shakespeare courses and an upper-level period class in the candidate’s area of expertise (e.g., Medieval, Renaissance, 18th century) Experience in writing studies and AI, with ability to teach first-year writing, a composition theory class, and contribute to campus discussions about writing pedagogy Application Instructions A complete application will include: Cover letter CV Statement of teaching philosophy Copy of graduate transcripts Contact information for three references Questions about the position may be directed to search chair Meg Gillette at meggillette@augustana.edu. To guarantee full consideration, please submit all application materials by October 15, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information The budgeted compensation for this position ranges from $60,000 to $63,000 per year based upon minimum and preferred qualifications, education, experience, skills, and abilities. Actual placement within the range will depend upon experience, education, research, and other relevant factors. Augustana College offers a competitive and comprehensive benefit package to its employees to ensure our team is well cared for. Benefits include: Medical, dental and vision insurance Retirement plan including eligibility to receive up to 7% contribution from the College. Company sponsored short-term and long-term disability benefits as use of college facilities including a wellness center, gym and recreation center. Tuition benefits for employees and their family members. You can learn more about our benefits program at our Benefits Website. Augustana College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Pay Range: $60,000 - $63,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78859fa064222601a0725f23f24c82": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands.  Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Description The Department of Music at Augustana College, Rock Island, Illinois, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands beginning in August of the 2027-2028 academic year. This is an exciting opportunity to conduct the esteemed Augustana Symphonic Band in its 153rd year and beyond, and to join a dynamic and committed department of teachers, performers, composers, and scholars, including sixteen full-time faculty members. We are passionately committed to mentoring and supporting undergraduate musicians of all skill levels, backgrounds, and academic majors. Augustana College is accredited by the National Association of Schools of Music (NASM). Responsibilities: Conduct Augustana Symphonic Band Teach in at least one other area depending on skills and interests (applied music, courses for music majors, general education courses) Oversee all activities related to bands at Augustana Carry a teaching load of 24 credits per 10-month academic year (standard courses are 2 or 4 credits) What We're Looking For High level of musicianship in the area of band conducting. Potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate students through bands and in at least one other area (applied music, courses for music majors, general education courses). Potential to develop an outstanding program of professional expression in music (e.g. as a performer, guest conductor, recording artist, clinician, etc.) Potential to oversee and develop a long-term vision for a vibrant, multiple-ensemble band program for music majors and non-majors, including national and international tours and meaningful community engagement. A completed DMA or equivalent in Band Conducting or a related field. ABD candidates will be considered. Why Augustana? At Augustana, you'll find a supportive and collegial environment where faculty thrive professionally and personally. Our small class sizes foster deep connections between faculty and students. You'll have access to resources and opportunities to pursue innovative research and impactful teaching. Application Instructions Requirements: A complete application will include: Cover letter CV A document with links to 2-3 videos of the candidate conducting a wind ensemble, including at least one rehearsal and at least one performance. Copy of graduate transcripts Contact information for three references Position Requirements A doctorate or ABD in band conducting Ability to lead a multi-ensemble band program and conducting the Augustana Symphonic Band Ability to teach courses in at least one other area Questions about the position may be directed to search chair Jacob Bancks at jacobbancks@augustana.edu. To guarantee full consideration, please submit all application materials by October 9, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Additional Information The budgeted compensation for this position ranges from $60,000 to $63,000 per year based upon minimum and preferred qualifications, education, experience, skills, and abilities. Actual placement within the range will depend upon experience, education, research, and other relevant factors. Augustana College offers a competitive and comprehensive benefit package to its employees to ensure our team is well cared for. Benefits include: Medical, dental and vision insurance Retirement plan including eligibility to receive up to 7% contribution from the College. Company sponsored short-term and long-term disability benefits as use of college facilities including a wellness center, gym and recreation center. Tuition benefits for employees and their family members. You can learn more about our benefits program at our Benefits Website. Augustana College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Pay Range: $60,000 - $63,000 per year APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a7887a1a150293901a15448aead1b28": {
      "title": "Assistant Track & Field Coach – Director of Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Track & Field Coach – Director of Operations.  Join Our Mission at Augustana College At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships—the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Assistant Track & Field Coach – Director of Operations Status: Exempt, full-time, 10-month schedule Reports To: Assistant Athletic Director for Leadership & Development Job Description: Overview: Is responsible for assisting in the overall management of the College's men's and women's track, field and cross-country programs, specifically the throws events. Duties include coaching, recruitment and retention of student-athletes, scheduling and budget management, equipment ordering, scheduling contests, viable fundraising, public relations, and other duties. Status: Full-time position. Works on an academic year schedule. Job Duties: Work under the direction of the Director of Cross Country/Track and Field to conduct and evaluate practice activities for designated team members. Provide group and individual assistance in a manner that engages the student-athletes and builds commitment to the program. Work collaboratively with the Director of Cross Country/Track and Field to integrate efforts and create program success. Assist other staff members with activities as needed to reach the goals of the team. Meet with prospective students and their family members both on campus and at remote locations. Provide advice and counsel on the admissions process, the Augustana experience and the integral role of the student-athlete in overall campus life. Align and promote the core principals and standards of the program at all times. Manage a diverse set of responsibilities including but not limited to assisting with travel arrangements, team travel meals, home event operations and other duties as assigned in relation to team operations. Provide feedback to assigned staff members and student workers on work performance and overall effectiveness. Create teaching curriculums for physical education activity courses as assigned during the academic year. Find ways to engage students in learning activities. Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Education: Bachelor's degree required, Master's degree preferred in a related field. Skills & Experience: 3(+) years experience in a coaching role, preferably at the small college level. Ability to understand and comply with a variety of regulations from the NCAA, CCIW as well as other regulatory bodies. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to interact with a diverse group of coaches, administrators, student athletes, prospective students and families and other members of the campus community. Strong prioritization and organizational skills. Must have a thorough understanding of and accountability to NCAA and CCIW rules and regulations. Strong commitment to the academic and athletic success of the student-athlete. Work Hours & Travel: This position requires travel to away contests during the season and to high school/club events, and other opportunities to meet with prospective students. Extended weekend and evening hours especially during the wrestling season are expected. Current valid driver's license required. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $40,000 - $42,000 annually commensurate with experience and qualifications. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Physical Requirements: This position is located on campus and works in a traditional office environment. The below requirements are expected: Must be able to lift 50 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Special Requirements: As key personnel representing the College, this position requires excellent interpersonal skills, the ability to relate to a diverse population, and the ability and willingness to model the mission and high standard of behavior of Augustana College. Successful candidates must pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $40,000 - $42,000 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78879ea15447f701a159852ff474d5": {
      "title": "Building Service Worker",
      "description": "Building Service Worker.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-onlearning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Building Service Worker/Custodian Status: Full-time, Non-Exempt position, calendar year schedule Wage Grade: 710 Reports To: Custodial Zone leader Overview: Under the general direction of the Custodial Zone Leader, custodians are responsible for the internal appearance of our buildings. It is important for custodians to be careful and thorough in working, cleaning and tidying the premises, as well as preventing vandalism. The ideal candidate will have previous custodial experience and be familiar with chemicals and equipment to complete the job efficiently and safely. Custodians must possess a high level of physical endurance to cover a large space as well as a keen eye for detail. Essential Job Duties: Cleans and maintains assigned areas on campus according to established school standards. Cleaning and maintenance duties frequently include vacuuming, mopping, and sweeping of floors, emptying trash, cleaning bathroom areas, window and door cleaning, snow and leaf removal, and other basic duties. Perform periodic deep cleaning duties as assigned which often include polishing and buffing of floors, shampoo of carpets, stripping and waxing of floors, window washing, and removal or moving of furniture. Set-up and tear down of designated spaces as needed including set-up and take down of tables, chairs and/or serving equipment. Work with other staff in a cooperative manner to accomplish tasks in designated area. Adapt to changing requests and supervisory instructions. Identify issues in assigned areas that need additional attention and communicate these needs to supervisory staff. Assist other staff members as needed or requested to ensure the campus meets highest possible cleanliness levels. Accomplishes all duties in accordance with established safety principles and guidelines. Work with other facilities staff members on special projects including cleaning of Transitional Living Areas, campus owned housing, and preparation of campus buildings for special events. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility: This position does not have direct supervisory responsibilities but does serve as a coach and mentor for student workers. Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of cleaning and/or maintenance experience in a team-based environment Excellent service orientation and ability to relate to a diverse campus population including co-workers, faculty members, students and visitors Willingness and ability to work with a variety of personalities and adapt to the changing needs of the campus, including a variety of work locations Skill in using a computer to communicate and complete work tasks. Ability to work with limited supervision and work effectively independently and as p 1-3 years of cleaning and/or maintenance experience in a team-based environment Excellent service orientation and ability to relate to a diverse campus population including co-workers, faculty members, students and visitors Willingness and ability to work with a variety of personalities and adapt to the changing needs of the campus, including a variety of work locations Skill in using a computer to communicate and complete work tasks. Ability to work with limited supervision and work effectively independently and as part of a team. Ability to work to high productivity standards with limited supervision Ability to utilize a radio for frequent communication including the ability to hear and speak clearly Education: High School Diploma or equivalent preferred. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.00 per hour. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Environment: This job operates in a varied work environment including time in an office environment, classroom environment and residential living areas, as well as some outdoor work. Limited exposure to extreme heat and cold weather conditions are expected. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift 50 pounds on a frequent basis and 75 pounds on an occasional basis. Must be able to push and pull heavy machinery on a frequent basis. This position requires frequent climbing of stairs and occasional work on ladders. Ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, , bend, stoop, and stand for long periods of time. Must possess finger and hand dexterity for using small tools and equipment. Ability to work outdoors for snow removal in the winter months and may experience extreme temperatures in non-air conditioned environments in the summer months. Expected hours of work: This is a Full-time position with a 40 hour work week working throughout a calendar year. Standard days and hours of work are Monday – Friday 5-6 a.m. through 1-2 p.m. On rare occasions and subject to supervisor approval, overtime may be required. Travel: Little to no travel is expected for this position. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $15 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78839ea150ae2901a16af5b746678e": {
      "title": "Campus Visit Coordinator",
      "description": "Campus Visit Coordinator.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Campus Visit Coordinator Status: Non-Exempt, Full-time 12 month schedule Wage Grade: 720 Reports To: Manager of Campus Visit Experience Position Overview: The Campus Visit Coordinator is the first point of contact for prospective students and their families, setting the tone for their experience with Augustana College. This role involves managing a fast-paced front office environment, providing exceptional customer service, and coordinating personalized campus visits. The coordinator supports the admissions team in delivering memorable, high-impact visit experiences that align with the college's recruitment goals. Key Responsibilities: Visitor Communication: ​Serve as the primary point of contact for prospective students, families, and campus partners, providing accurate and friendly communication via phone, email, and in-person interactions. ​Record and track interactions in the student information system, ensuring timely follow-up and accurate data management. Visit Coordination: Prepare personalized visit materials, including name tags, agendas, and information packets. Create working visit agendas, coordinating schedules for counselor meetings, campus tour guides and meeting rooms. Plan and execute group visits for school groups, field trips, and special events. Schedule and coordinate athletic visit requests from coaching staff. Student Staff Supervision: Supervise a team of student Campus Visit Assistants, providing training, work direction, and ongoing support. Collaborate with student workers to ensure a seamless and positive visitor experience. Office Support and Administration: Support the Manager of Campus Visit Experience in scheduling visitor appointments and coordinating faculty, coach, and counselor availability. Provide additional support to admissions staff, including data entry, mail distribution, and office organization. Maintain an organized inventory of visit supplies and office materials. Event Support: Assist incoming students with questions related to Orientation and Registration events. Contribute to the planning and execution of large-scale visit events and special programs. Problem-Solving and Professionalism: Resolve scheduling conflicts and other issues independently, maintaining a professional and solutions-oriented approach. Act as a resource for colleagues, providing insights and support as needed to enhance the campus visit experience. Other Duties as Assigned: Participate in special projects and support other admissions initiatives as needed. Skills & Experience: Customer Service & Communication: 1-3 years of experience in customer service, including phone, email, and face-to-face interactions, with a demonstrated ability to make a positive first impression. Event Planning & Coordination: Experience organizing and coordinating complex schedules and events, including group visits, presentations, and multi-step visitor agendas. Technical Proficiency: Strong computer skills with intermediate knowledge of the Google Suite (Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Drive, Docs, Sheets) and experience with data entry and management in a CRM (e.g., Slate) preferred. Leadership & Supervision: Experience working with or supervising student employees, providing direction, training, and mentorship to ensure high-quality visitor experiences. Organizational Skills: Excellent prioritization and time management skills, with the ability to handle multiple projects and deadlines in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions. Attention to Detail: Highly detail-oriented, with a track record of accuracy and thoroughness in materials preparation and data management. Problem-Solving & Decision-Making: Strong critical thinking skills, with the ability to independently resolve scheduling conflicts and other unexpected challenges in a professional and timely manner. Team Collaboration: Ability to build and maintain strong, collaborative relationships with colleagues across the admissions team and other campus departments. Professionalism & Flexibility: Comfortable working independently and as part of a team, with a proactive, solutions-focused approach to daily responsibilities. Education: High School diploma or GED required. Advanced education or 1-3 years of customer service, event planning, or college admissions experience is highly preferred. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.45 per hour. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Physical Requirements: Must be able to lift 25 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Special Requirements: As key personnel representing the College, this position requires excellent interpersonal skills, the ability to relate to a diverse population, and the ability and willingness to model the mission and high standard of behavior of Augustana College. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $15.45 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78839ea150ae2901a16ada44fc6410": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Title: Financial Aid Counselor Status: Non-Exempt Full-time, 12 month schedule Wage: 735H Reports To: Assistant Director of Financial Aid Overview: Using information from a variety of sources including submitted records and personal interviews, evaluates financial needs of students. Awards financial aid according to government and institutional regulations and guidelines. Works collaboratively with others in the office to achieve timely communication with all potential students and manages workflow to meet deadlines in a high volume processing environment Primary Duties: Counsels and advises students about financial aid eligibility, application procedures, aid programs, aid eligibility, packaging policies, costs, billing process, indebtedness. Also provides general information via e-mail, phone, and personal contact. Analyzes student files to make an independent determination for financial aid and then reviews, awards, verifies and processes financial aid paperwork. Independently conducts analysis on students who have had their FAFSA selected for verification, determines and requests additional documentation as needed. Submits corrections to the Department of Education, evaluates eligibility and changes awards if necessary. Answers questions, inquiries or requests from students or parents in person, by phone or in writing regarding financial aid programs and eligibility. Assists in the preparation and presentation of information regarding federal financial aid, scholarships, employment and grants for various campus groups, high school students and parents at meetings, group discussions, workshops and recruitment sessions. Analyzes various system generated reports such as grades and enrollment status or award status to verify continued compliance and eligibility of students receiving aid under federal and institutional guidelines; notifies students of changes in eligibility of awards and alternatives to amend the situation. Additional Duties: Interfaces with students, employers, donors, and/or staff to resolve issues. Assists with other financial aid activities such as outreach, reporting and monitoring. Regular activities require ability to quickly change priorities and may include and/or are subject to resolution conflict. Other duties as assigned Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of experience in a professional setting with a focus on communication, customer service and/or counseling skills. Prior experience with FAFSA or other financial aid related experience preferred. Strong attention to detail with excellent financial acumen. Ability to organize and manage multiple projects while working in a high-pressure, fast paced and frequently changing environment. Basic understanding or ability to learn government, donor and/or institutional rules, regulations, guidelines, and procedures for awarding of financial aid. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office products including experience working with Word, Excel and PowerPoint, as well as ability to quickly learn the Ellucian Colleague system. Patience, high energy, enthusiasm for helping others. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality. Ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with a diverse constituency of parents, students, campus colleagues and visitors. Strong problem solving skills. Ability to work independently with limited supervision. Education: Bachelor’s degree in a related field. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $20.65 - $25.25 per hour, commensurate with experience and qualifications. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website Work Environment: This position works in a traditional office environment. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift 15 pounds on an occasional basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Expected hours of work: This position works a 40 hour work week during the academic year as well as the summer. Hours typically are 8am – 4:30pm. During heavy financial aid awarding “season” evening and weekend work is required to meet department goals. Travel: Little to no travel is expected for this position EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $20.65 - $25.25 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78839fa14d56d401a15465d2f13b7c": {
      "title": "Full Time Administrative Assistant - Academic Year",
      "description": "Full Time Administrative Assistant - Academic Year.  At Augustana College, we don’t just educate students - we empower them. As a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences, we invest in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and building strong community partnerships, the driving forces of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students, Augustana offers a collaborative and student-focused environment, in which faculty and staff play an active role in shaping futures through hands-on learning, mentorship and leadership development. Located on a scenic, wooded campus in Rock Island, Illinois, Augustana is part of the vibrant Quad-Cities metropolitan area (pop. 470,000), about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. We seek mission-driven professionals who are passionate about student success, innovation and making an impact. If you thrive in an environment that values curiosity, collaboration and the power of transformative education, we invite you to bring your talents to Augustana. Administrative Assistant - Full-Time Academic Year Opportunities Join our dynamic academic team as an Administrative Assistant supporting one of our college's academic departments. This role follows the academic calendar, working from late August through the end of May, with summers off - perfect for those seeking a balanced work-life rhythm aligned with the school year. If you're organized, collaborative, and enjoy supporting faculty, staff and students we encourage you to apply! Job Title: Academic Administrative Assistant Status: Non-Exempt, Full-Time Academic Year Wage Grade: 720 Reports To: Academic Department Chair(s) Primary Duties: Answers phone calls, greets visitors and provides a warm welcome while meeting the needs of students, faculty members, and others interacting with the designated academic departments. Provides basic services for students & faculty members including copying of class materials, preparing documents and providing information about activities and offerings of the department. Responsible for the hiring, training and supervision of student workers as needed. Assigns projects, creates schedules, and communicates expectations. Maintains electronic student worker time cards and submits these to payroll in a timely manner. Maintains and updates the department websites and social media postings. Oversees departmental financial management such as reconciling P-cards, managing the departmental budget and paying invoices. Plans and coordinates special events such as banquets, open houses, faculty interviews, guest speakers, and other events. Oversees and maintains adequate supplies of office materials and other needs for the department Serve as backup administrative support to other departments as needed. Assists with special projects, events and other duties as assigned. Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of demonstrated experience providing administrative support for a variety of individuals. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Excellent computer skills with a working knowledge of Microsoft Office products and ability to learn Web basics. Ability to work with limited supervision, prioritize work, and meet deadlines with a high degree of detail orientation and accuracy. Excellent customer service skills and ability to work with a diverse group of colleagues, faculty members, members of the campus community, students and parents. Time management skills to handle multiple priorities in an environment of frequent interruptions. Education: High School Diploma or GED required. Additional education preferred. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.45 per hour. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. Work Environment: This position works in a standard office environment. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift 25 pounds on a frequent basis. Also required is the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must be able to use a computer to accomplish a variety of job tasks. Expected hours of work: Academic Year / 40 hours per week This is a full time position with a 40 hour work week. Standard days and hours of work are Monday – Friday 8:00 a.m. through 4:30pm during the academic year. On rare occasions and subject to supervisor approval, overtime may be required. Travel: Little to no travel is expected for this position. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities are subject to change at any time with or without notice. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and names of 3 references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $15.45 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68e824f98018e86e912830214&id=8a78839fa1559acc01a15f0c3ce724f4": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Groundskeeper.  About Augustana College Augustana College is a nationally recognized college of the liberal arts and sciences dedicated to investing in engaged learning, maximizing student potential, and strengthening community partnerships - the guiding priorities of our Bold & Boundless Strategic Plan (2024-29). For our 2,500 students from all backgrounds, Augustana provides a transformative experience that integrates rigorous academics, hands-on learning and mentorship to prepare graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. The college’s scenic, wooded campus is located in Rock Island, Illinois, part of the Quad-Cities metro area (pop. 470,000) along the Mississippi River, about a 3-hour drive from Chicago. At Augustana, we seek innovative and student-centered professionals who are excited to contribute to our strategic goals of empowering students through engaged learning, leadership development and real-world experiences. Employees at Augustana enjoy an excellent benefit package including medical, retirement, generous paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and their family members, and much more. Job Description: Job Title: Groundskeeper Status: Regular Full-time Non-Exempt - Year round, ongoing 12 month schedule Wage: 710 Reports To: Grounds Manager Overview: Works collaboratively with other members of the grounds staff to maintain the grounds of Augustana College in a safe manner. Primary duties include mowing, snow removal, landscape maintenance, trash collection, tree removal and removal of leaves and debris. Job Duties: Responsible for the maintenance of assigned areas on campus which may include trash pick-up, snow removal, grass cutting, pruning, clipping, raking, leaf removal, as well as other duties. Mows turf areas as assigned throughout campus using a walk-behind mower. Plants and transplants trees, shrubs and other plants. Waters, mulches, plants and maintains annual and perennial planting areas. Responsible for assigned turf renovations including seeding, sodding, aeration and watering. Removes trash, leaves, and debris throughout campus as well as campus owned housing areas. Maintains and repairs on campus irrigation systems. Removes snow and ice from campus walk ways and parking lots using shovels as well as power equipment. Uses supplies and equipment as instructed, following College guidelines for safety. Is aware of and operates within OSHA standards and guidelines at all times. Works collaboratively with other grounds crew members and student workers as well as other departments to meet the overall goals of the College. Assist campus visitors with requests and instructions in a courteous and helpful manner that reflects the high standards of Augustana. Responds to emergency situations as needed. Reports unusual issues or problems to the supervisor in a timely manner. Other duties as assigned Requirements: Education: GED or High School Diploma required Skills & Experience: 1-3 years of related experience Ability to work with limited supervision Ability to safely operate a variety of power equipment with basic training including but not limited to: manual transmission dump truck, mowers, hand tools, gas powered blower, snow blower, string trimmers, chain saw. Ability to follow standard practices and safety regulations Ability to work collaboratively with a wide variety of personalities. Physical Requirements: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Must be able to lift and/or move 50 pounds on a frequent basis and occasionally lift and/or move 75+ pounds. Must have the ability to listen, hear, speak, read, write, climb stairs, bend, stoop, and stand for intermittently long periods of time. Must possess finger and hand dexterity for using small tools and equipment. Overtime required for snow and ice removal, special events and emergencies. Work Environment: The employee is regularly exposed to outside weather conditions and occasionally exposed to moving mechanical parts, fumes or airborne particles and moderate noise levels. Frequent exposure to extreme heat and cold weather conditions. Special Requirements: A valid driver's license is required. Successful candidates must pass a criminal background check. Additional Information: Pay and Benefits: This position is budgeted to pay $15.00 per hour. We offer a competitive benefits package designed to support the needs of employees. Full-time employees are eligible for a comprehensive range of benefits including: Medical, dental, vision insurance Flexible spending accounts or health savings accounts Life insurance, disability insurance, and supplemental insurance programs Retirement plan with a generous company contribution Excellent paid time off/holiday benefits Tuition benefits for employees and their family members Access to company facilities (gym, pool, health center, etc.) You can learn more about our benefit programs at our Benefits website. EEO Statement: Augustana is an Equal Opportunity Employer. It is Augustana College’s policy to provide equal opportunity to all qualified employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability and any other category protected by federal, state or local law. Note: This job description is subject to change and is not designed to be a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required by the employee. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit a resume and cover letter. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States; this position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Pay Range: $15 per hour APPLY FOR THIS POSITION Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    }
  },
